 ## Overview
-Importance-Based Accumulated Transparency Modulation (IBATM) is a volume rendering compositing technique that highlights specific features by modulating accumulated transparency based on the difference between an importance measure of the incoming sample and the accumulated result along a viewing ray [S1]. Unlike its predecessor Maximum Intensity Difference Accumulation (MIDA), which modulates accumulated color, IBATM modulates only accumulated transparency, thereby avoiding color values exceeding unity and the need for complex tone-mapping within the core algorithm [S1]. It builds on [Front-to-Back Compositing (Over Operator)](3360-front-to-back-compositing-over-operator.md) by inserting a transparency modulation step before the standard over-operator blend.
